It comes and goes, but there never seems to have been enough of a driver for anyone to spec it out.  The idea of all responses being an object is that there can be metadta next to the `data` key, that so if an implementation wanted to implement pagination the relevant keys could be placed in to the top-level response, _e.g._

```
{
  "data": [ ... ],
  "pagination": {
    "next_cursor": "abc123",
    ...
  }
}
```
